<title>SINGAPORE: Hwa Tat Lee first half loss at S$1.9 mln.</title>
<headline>Hwa Tat Lee first half loss at S$1.9 mln.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended June 30 1996</p>
<p>	   (in millions of S$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit		   (1.89)     vs    (2.35)</p>
<p>    Group shares (cents)     (1.27)     vs    (1.59)</p>
<p>    Turnover		     37.70	vs    41.61</p>
<p>    Other income		  0.07	vs     0.07</p>
<p>    Interest on borrowings    1.09	vs     0.93</p>
<p>    Depreciation/amortisation 2.91	vs     1.94</p>
<p>    Pre-tax			(1.67)     vs    (1.86)</p>
<p>    Associates		    0.02	vs    (0.02)</p>
<p>    Tax			     0.24	vs     0.45</p>
<p>Furniture maker Hwa Tat Lee Holdings Ltd said it expect second half performance to improve.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703080)</p>
</text>
